.TH CHTTP_METHOD_STR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_method_str \- return the canonical string for an HTTP method
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttp.h>

const char *chttp_method_str(chttp_method_t m);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the uppercase ASCII method string for the given enum value
(e.g. "GET", "POST").  Returns "ANY" for CHTTP_ANY (a server-side
routing sentinel, not a real HTTP method).  Falls back to "UNKNOWN"
for invalid values.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Pointer to a static string literal; must not be freed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_method_t (3)
